# Local environment for docker-compose.yml.
#
# No variables are required: the stack runs with its built-in defaults
# (loopback-only, authenticated single-node MongoDB replica set and
# PLAINTEXT Kafka — see the SECURITY NOTE at the top of docker-compose.yml).
#
# To override the MongoDB credentials, copy this file to `.env` (docker
# compose reads `.env` automatically) and set:
#
#   MONGO_USER=root
#   MONGO_PASSWORD=devpass123
#
# Defaults when unset: MONGO_USER=root, MONGO_PASSWORD=devpass123.
#
# IMPORTANT: changing the credentials only takes effect on a fresh mongo
# volume — the root user is created by the image entrypoint on first init
# (empty data volume only). If you change them after the first `up`, also
# run `docker compose down --volumes` first (wipes local dev data).
#
# If you do not run anything else on the same host, the mapped ports
# (API 8090, MongoDB 27018, Kafka 29092) work out of the box. To change a
# port, edit docker-compose.yml directly (the ports are not variableized so
# the scaffold stays minimal).
#
# SECURITY: this is a local development scaffold. It must not be exposed
# beyond localhost. Production deployments need real credentials (secret
# manager / vault, never a checked-in .env), a multi-node replica set, and
# Kafka SASL/SCRAM (+ mTLS at the edges).
